invariant: INV-43
file: p256_wide_verify.c
catches: proof/prove-one.sh p256_wide_verify
reason: the host verifier computes on whatever the decoder left for a key
  it refused: a coordinate at or above p, or a pair off the curve. The
  words are then no point, and their X matches r one time in 2^256, so
  bin/p256_verify_equiv_test passes on its keys off the curve. The
  proof's stub of the decoder answers either verdict, and the proof
  requires the verdict 0 when it refuses.

--- old
    if (p256_wide_point_from_bytes(&q, encoded) == 0) {
        return 0;
    }
--- new
    (void)p256_wide_point_from_bytes(&q, encoded);
